      "page_title": "Exit Codes, OOM Kills and Disk Cleanup",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Worked Example",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker ps -a",
            "docker logs --tail 100 api",
            "docker inspect api \\",
            "  --format '{{.State.OOMKilled}}'",
            "docker run -m 512m api:1.0"
          ],
          "note": "OOMKilled true means raise --memory",
          "result": {
            "headers": [
              "Check",
              "Output"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "ps -a",
                "Exited (137)"
              ],
              [
                "OOMKilled",
                "true"
              ],
              [
                "Fix",
                "raise --memory"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Check `State.OOMKilled` in `docker inspect`",
            "Raise `--memory`, or fix the **leak**",
            "Restart loop: check logs, CMD, ENTRYPOINT",
            "Also check missing env vars and port conflicts"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Reclaim Disk Space",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker system df` shows what Docker uses",
            "`docker system prune` removes dangling images, stopped containers",
            "It also clears unused build cache"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Exit 0 at once: main process finished or went to background",
            "A container lives only as long as **PID 1**",
            "Logging to a file, so `docker logs` stays empty",
            "Guessing the cause before reading the exit code"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Live Inspection",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker stats` shows live CPU, memory and network",
            "`docker top` lists the processes in a container",
            "`docker events` streams ==daemon activity== as it happens"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
