    {
      "page_title": "Restarts, Graceful Stop and Orchestrators",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Stay Up and Healthy",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--restart unless-stopped` or `always` revives containers after a crash or reboot",
            "Add ==HEALTHCHECK== so the platform sees a hung app, not just an exit",
            "`--memory` and `--cpus` stop one container **starving** the host"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker run -d --init \\",
            "  --restart unless-stopped \\",
            "  --memory 512m --cpus 1.5 \\",
            "  --log-opt max-size=10m \\",
            "  --log-opt max-file=3 app:1.0"
          ],
          "note": "restart only reacts to exit, not hangs"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Stop Gracefully",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "docker stop",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "SIGTERM",
                "sub": "to PID 1",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "App drains",
                "sub": "close, flush",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "Exit 0",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "SIGKILL",
                "sub": "after 10s",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "App must ==handle SIGTERM==: finish requests, close connections, then exit",
            "Use exec-form `CMD [\"app\"]` so the app itself is PID 1",
            "`--init` (tini) forwards signals and **reaps** zombie processes"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "# exec form: node is PID 1",
            "CMD [\"node\", \"server.js\"]",
            "HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s \\",
            "  --retries=3 \\",
            "  CMD curl -f localhost/up \\",
            "   || exit 1"
          ],
          "note": "shell-form CMD hides SIGTERM from app"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Logs and 12-Factor",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Log driver `json-file` grows forever: set `max-size` and `max-file`",
            "Ship logs to a ==central system==, not the host disk",
            "Config comes from **environment** variables, never baked into the image",
            "Stateless containers, one process each, logs written to stdout"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Orchestrators",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Add scheduling, self-healing, rolling updates and service discovery",
            "Also add autoscaling and managed ==secrets==",
            "Swarm clusters hosts with `docker stack deploy`; Kubernetes is the standard"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Scope",
            "Effort"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Compose",
              "{green:Single host}",
              "{green:Low}"
            ],
            [
              "Swarm",
              "{orange:Simple multi-host}",
              "{orange:Medium}"
            ],
            [
              "Kubernetes",
              "{red:Powerful, any scale}",
              "{red:High, complex}"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "solid"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "aside": "ship it safely!",
      "subtitle": "Run it, stop it, scale it"
