    {
      "page_title": "Interview Answers: Isolation, Image Size and Run Flow",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Image vs Container",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Trait",
            "Image",
            "Container"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Mode",
              "{blue:read-only template}",
              "{green:writable layer on top}"
            ],
            [
              "Nature",
              "==immutable== and layered",
              "a **running** instance"
            ],
            [
              "Count",
              "one image",
              "many containers from it"
            ],
            [
              "Created by",
              "`docker build`",
              "`docker run`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How Docker Isolates",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Namespaces== decide what a process can **see**",
            "Namespaces: pid, net, mnt, uts, ipc, user",
            "==cgroups== cap what a process can **use**",
            "cgroups limit CPU, memory, I/O and pids"
          ],
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Reduce Image Size",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Use ==multi-stage builds==: ship only the artifact",
            "Pick a **slim** or distroless base image",
            "Add a `.dockerignore` to trim the build context",
            "Combine `RUN` steps and clean up in one layer"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM golang:1.22 AS build",
            "COPY . .",
            "RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -o /app",
            "FROM gcr.io/distroless/static:nonroot",
            "COPY --from=build /app /app",
            "ENTRYPOINT [\"/app\"]"
          ],
          "note": "Without .dockerignore, COPY . . leaks .git"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Persist and Connect",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Persist with ==named volumes== or bind mounts",
            "The container layer is **gone** after `docker rm`",
            "Containers talk over a ==user-defined network==",
            "Service-name DNS: `http://db:5432` just works",
            "The default bridge gives IPs but no name lookup"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. What docker run nginx Does",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "CLI",
                "sub": "calls dockerd",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Pull",
                "sub": "if image missing",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "Create",
                "sub": "rw layer, network",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "runc",
                "sub": "namespaces, cgroups",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "nginx",
                "sub": "starts as PID 1",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Build Best Practices",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Pin== base image versions, never bare `latest`",
            "Put **rarely-changing** instructions first for cache hits",
            "Keep a `.dockerignore` for node_modules, .git, .env",
            "Prefer `COPY` over `ADD`",
            "==Scan== images in CI before they ship"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Run Best Practices",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One concern per container, one process each",
            "Run as ==non-root== with `USER app`",
            "**Log to stdout**, not to files",
            "Add a `HEALTHCHECK` so failures are detected",
            "Handle ==SIGTERM== and set resource limits"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "aside": "say it in one line",
      "subtitle": "Answers worth memorizing"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Interview Pitfalls and Digest-Pinned Deploys",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mistakes to Avoid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Baking secrets into ENV or layers: ==never store secrets in images==",
            "Shipping only `latest`: tag releases with ==git SHA + semver==, like `1.4.2-a1b2c3d`",
            "Letting one container take all host memory",
            "Using a fat base image for a tiny binary"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Reproducible Deploys",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`name:tag` is a mutable pointer; it can move",
            "Pin by ==digest==: `image@sha256:...` never changes",
            "Multi-arch: `docker buildx build --platform`"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Mounting docker.sock?",
          "text": "It gives that container root-equivalent control of the host."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "Walk through what happens on `docker run nginx`.",
            "How would you containerize and ship a service end to end?"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "Small pinned non-root images, volumes for data, stdout logs and SHA tags."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Answers worth memorizing"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Build, Inspect and Cleanup Commands",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Build and run",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker build -t app:1.0 .",
            "docker run -d -p 8080:80 \\",
            "  --name app app:1.0",
            "docker exec -it app sh"
          ],
          "note": "-d detached, -p host:container"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`-d`",
              "run detached"
            ],
            [
              "`-p 8080:80`",
              "publish host:container port"
            ],
            [
              "`--name`",
              "give the container a name"
            ],
            [
              "`--rm`",
              "delete it on exit"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker run` starts a **new** container",
            "`docker exec` enters a ==running== one",
            "`docker stop`: SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after 10s",
            "`docker kill` sends SIGKILL immediately"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Inspect",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker ps -a",
            "docker logs -f app",
            "docker inspect app",
            "docker stats",
            "docker top app"
          ],
          "note": "ps -a also lists stopped ones"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Pull one field",
          "text": "Use `docker inspect --format` to extract just the field you need."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Cleanup",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker rm -f app",
            "docker rmi app:1.0",
            "docker system prune -a",
            "docker volume prune"
          ],
          "note": "prune -a deletes unused images"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Safe cleanup",
          "text": "Run `docker system df` first, and keep `prune -a` for last."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Volumes and networks",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker volume create v",
            "docker network create n",
            "docker run -v v:/data \\",
            "  --network n app:1.0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Named volume `v` keeps data after `docker rm`",
            "User-defined network `n` adds DNS by container name",
            "Reach other services by name, never `localhost`"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mount",
            "Best for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{green:Volume}",
              "production data, backups"
            ],
            [
              "{blue:Bind mount}",
              "live-reload development"
            ],
            [
              "{orange:tmpfs}",
              "secrets, scratch in memory"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "aside": "tear this out!",
      "subtitle": "Commands at a glance"
